       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use.\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg at once is double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 400 mg by mouth four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1600 mg total per day, divided into several doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do intend 1600 mg four times daily, confirm that and tell me the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
